{#
  What a citation says of the page it cites: its name and its author, the part
  of the line after "In reply to", "Liked" and the rest. Shared by
  `reply-context.njk` and `citations.njk` (TASK-247).

    {% import "partials/cited-page.njk" as cited %}
    {{ cited.page(inReplyTo, replyContext) }}

  `url` is the cited page, always its `u-url`. `context` is what the page said
  about itself, from the reply contexts file. With a name, the name is the
  link; with only an author, "a post" is; with neither, the bare URL. The
  author follows as an `h-card`.

  A name that already ends in " by " and the author's name, matched without
  regard to case (SoundCloud's oEmbed gives "Flickermood by Forss" by Forss),
  is not followed by the author again. Its last words become the `h-card`,
  printed as the title wrote them, and the whole name stays the `p-name`, so a
  parser reads the same name and author either way.
#}
{% macro page(url, context) %}
{%- set title = (context.name or "") | trim -%}
{%- set author = (context.author.name or "") | trim if context.author else "" -%}
{%- set cut = title.length - author.length - 4 -%}
{%- set byline = title.slice(cut) if (author and cut > 0) else "" -%}
{%- set named = byline and byline.slice(0, 4).toLowerCase() == " by " and byline.slice(4).toLowerCase() == author.toLowerCase() -%}
{%- if named %} <span class="p-name"><a class="u-url" href="{{ url }}">{{ title.slice(0, cut) }}</a>{{ byline.slice(0, 4) }}{{ card(context.author, byline.slice(4)) }}</span>
{%- else %}
  {%- if context.name %} <a class="u-url p-name" href="{{ url }}">{{ context.name }}</a>
  {%- elif context.author %} <a class="u-url" href="{{ url }}">a post</a>
  {%- else %} <a class="u-url" href="{{ url }}">{{ url }}</a>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if context.author %} by {{ card(context.author, context.author.name) }}{% endif %}
{%- endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro card(author, name) -%}
<span class="p-author h-card">
  {%- if author.url %}<a class="u-url p-name" href="{{ author.url }}">{{ name }}</a>
  {%- else %}<span class="p-name">{{ name }}</span>{% endif -%}
</span>
{%- endmacro %}
